          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            induces a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            over
            %em paths
            \. A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} connection on a 2-bundle
            induces a generalization of this to a notion of parallel transport over
            %em surfaces
            \. Similarly a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+3-bundle"} connection on a 3-bundle
            induces a notion of parallel transport over 3-dimensional volumes.
          %p
            Generally, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on an ∞-bundle
            induces a notion of parallel transport in arbitrary dimension.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The higher notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
            make sense in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Disc
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Π
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Top
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi \dashv Disc \dashv \Gamma) :
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}}
                  \\infty Grpd \simeq Top
                  \\,.
          %p
            In every such there is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on an ∞-bundle
            and of its higher parallel transport.
          %p
            A typical context considered (more or less explicitly) in the literature is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
          %h3#higher_parallel_transport Higher parallel transport
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            such that morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to A
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            classify the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{conn}
            for the differential refinement described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+form"} ∞-Lie algebra valued form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; A_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; A
                  }
          %p
            describe
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} connections on ∞-bundles
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              %strong
                admits parallel
                = succeed "-transport" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              if for all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and all morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi : \Sigma \to X
            %p
              we have that the pullback of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∇
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi^* \nabla : \Sigma \stackrel{\phi}{\to} X \stackrel{\nabla}{\to} A_{conn}
            %p
              %strong flat
              in that it factors through the canonical inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi conn
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}A \to A_{conn}
            %p
              In other words: if all the lower
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              = succeed "-forms," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq k \leq n
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* \nabla
              vanish (the higher ones vanish automatically for dimensional reasons).
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mo ♭
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}A = [\mathbf{\Pi}(-),A]
            is the coefficient for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} flat differential A-cohomology
          .un_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This condition is automatically satisfied for ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+bundles"} connections on bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbf{B}G
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              an ordinary
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              2-form.
            %p
              But for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
              with connection there is in general a 2-form curvature and a 3-form curvature. A 2-connection therefore admits parallel transport only if its 2-form curvature is constrained to vanish.
            %p
              Notice however that if the coefficient object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              happens to be
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              – for instance if it is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+object"} Eilenberg-MacLane object
              in degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %em every
              connection admits parallel transport. This is notably the case for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla : X \to A_{conn}
              an
              = succeed "-connection" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "-transport," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\Pi}(\Sigma) \to A
            %p
              that corresponds to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* \nabla
              under the equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}(\Sigma, \mathbf{\flat}A ) \simeq \mathbf{H}(\mathbf{\Pi}(\Sigma), A)
                    \\,.
          .un_defn
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The objects of the
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity%2C1)-topos#Paths"} path ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}(\Sigma)
              are points in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}(\Sigma) \to A
              assigns fibers in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to points in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %h3#higher_holonomy Higher holonomy
          %p
            We now define the higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogs"} analogs
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is closed.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla : X \to A_{conn}
              be a connection with parallel
              = succeed "-transport" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
              a morphism from a
              %em closed
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
