            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\phi^* \nabla] \in [\Pi(\Sigma), \Gamma(A)]
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#for_trivial_circle_bundles__for_forms
            For trivial circle
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The simplest example is the parallel transport in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            whose underlying
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{n-1}U(1)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^n(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma_n \to X
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            from an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} tra
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tra_A(\Sigma) = \exp(i \int_\Sigma \phi^* A)
                  \\;\;\; \in \;\; U(1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            One can understand higher parallel transport therefore as a generalization of integration of differential
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-form" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-form" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                but more generally is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid+valued+differential+form"} ∞-Lie algebroid valued differential form
          %h3#for_circle_bundles_with_connection
            For circle
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            We show how the
            = succeed "-holonomy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            is reproduced from the above.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* \nabla : \mathbf{\Pi}(\Sigma) \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            be the parallel transport for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            over a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
          %p This is equivalent to a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi(\Sigma) \to \mathcal{B}^n U(1)
                  ,.
          %p
            We may map this further to its
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi dim
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-dim \Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo :
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mi Σ
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \:\infty Grpd(\Pi(\Sigma), \mathcal{B}^n U(1))
                  \\to
                  \\tau_{n-dim \Sigma} \infty Grpd(\Pi(X), \mathcal{B}^n U(1))
                  \\,.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p We have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi dim
                        %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi dim
                        %mi Σ
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_{n-dim\Sigma} \infty Grpd(\Pi(\Sigma), \mathcal{B}^n U(1))
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbf{B}^{n-dim \Sigma} U(1)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (This is due to an observation by
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"} Domenico Fiorenza
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By general abstract reasoning (recalled at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_i \infty Grpd(\Pi(\Sigma),\mathcal{B}^n U(1))
                    \\simeq
                    H^{n-i}(\Sigma, U(1))
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now use the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ext
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\to
                    Ext^1(H_{n-i-1}(\Sigma,\mathbb{Z}),U(1))
                    \\to
                    H^{n-i}(\Sigma,U(1))
                    \\to
                    Hom(H_{n-i}(\Sigma,\mathbb{Z}),U(1))
                    \\to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ext
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ext^1(-,U(1))=0
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^{n-i}(\Sigma,U(1))
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{Ab}(H_{n-i}(\Sigma,\mathbb{Z}),U(1))
            %p
              that identifies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
              in question with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              from the integral
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
              group of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\lt (n-dim \Sigma)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi for
                    %mi i
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi dim
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_i \infty Grpd(\Pi(\Sigma),\mathbf{B}^n U(1)) =0 \;\;\;\;
                    for i\lt (n-dim \Sigma)
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=(n-dim \Sigma)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{n-i}(\Sigma,\mathbb{Z})\simeq \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is a closed
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim \Sigma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi dim
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_{(n-dim\Sigma)} \infty Grpd(\Pi(\Sigma),\mathcal{B}^n U(1))\simeq U(1)
                    \\,.
          .un_def
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p The resulting morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi conn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi exp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi dim
                        %mi Σ
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}(\Sigma, A_{conn})
                    \\stackrel{\exp(i S(-))}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{B}^{n-dim\Sigma} U(1)
            %p
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              we call the
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-Chern-Simons action
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            Here in the language of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi conn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(\Sigma,A_{conn})
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi conn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(\Sigma, A_{conn})
                are the
                = succeed "s;." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
          %h3#nonabelian_parallel_transport_in_low_dimension Nonabelian parallel transport in low dimension
          %p
            At least in low categorical dimension one has the definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+n-groupoid"} path n-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}_n(X)
            of a smooth manifold, whose
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-classes" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+homotopy"} thin homotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]^n \to X
            = succeed "-transport" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-curvature" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}_n
            (
            %a{:href => "#SWI"}> SWI
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SWII"} SWII
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MartinsPickenI"} MartinsPickenI
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MartinsPickenII"} MartinsPickenII
          %h4#1transport 1-Transport
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
          %h4#2transport 2-Transport
          %p
            We work now concretely in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi DiffeoGrpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2DiffeoGrpd
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
            the category of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn 2
                  %mi DiffeoGrpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}_2(X) \in 2DiffeoGrpd
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+2-groupoid"} path 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-group"} Lie 2-group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn 2
                  %mi DiffeoGrpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \in 2DiffeoGrpd
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            1-object 2-groupoid. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
          %p
            Assume now first that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_1 \to G_0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+crossed+module"} differential crossed module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}_1 \to \mathfrak{g}_0)
          %p We describe now how smooth 2-functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tra : \mathbf{P}_2(X) \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            i.e. morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi DiffeoGrpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2DiffeoGrpd
            are characterized by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra+valued+differential+forms"} Lie 2-algebra valued differential forms
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Given a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathbf{P}_2(X) \to \mathbf{B}G
              we construct a
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_F \in \Omega^2(X, \mathfrak{g}_1)
              as follows.
            %p
              To find the value of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_F
              on two vectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi p
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1, v_2 \in T_p X
              at some point,
              %em choose
              any smooth function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma : \mathbb{R}^2 \to X
            %p with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(0,0) = p
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{d}{d s}|_{s = 0} \Gamma(s,0) = v_1
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mi t
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{d}{d t}|_{t = 0} \Gamma(0,t) = v_2
                  \.
            %p Notice that there is a canonical 2-parameter family
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mor
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma_{\mathbb{R}} : \mathbb{R}^2 \to 2Mor \mathbf{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^2)
            %p
              of classes of bigons on the plane, given by sending
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t) \in \mathbb{R}^2
              to the class represented by any bigon (with sitting instants) with straight edges filling the square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi s
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi s
                              %mo ,
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma_{\mathbb{R}}(s,t) =
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    (0,0) &amp;\to&amp; (0,t)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    (s,0) &amp;\to&amp; (s,t)
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Using this we obtain a smooth function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mor
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo *
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mor
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_\Gamma :
                    \\mathbb{R}^2 \stackrel{\Sigma_{\mathbb{R}}}{\to}
                    2Mor \mathbf{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^2)
                    \\stackrel{\Gamma_*}{\to}
                    2Mor \mathbf{P}_2(X)
                    \\stackrel{F}{\to}
                    G_0 \times G_1
                    \\stackrel{p_2}{\to}
                    G_1
                    \\,.
            %p Then set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B_F(v_1, w_1) :=
                    \\frac{\partial^2 F_\Gamma}{\partial x \partial y}|_{(0,0)}
                    \\,.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              This is well defined, in that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_F(v_1,v_2)
              does not depend on the choices made. Moreover, the 2-form defines this way is smooth.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              To see that the definition does not depend on the choice of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %p
              For given vectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} T
                      %mi X
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1,v_2 \in \T_X X
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma, \Gamma' : \mathbb{R}^2 \to X
              be two choices of smooth maps as in the defnition. By restricting, if necessary, to a neighbourhood of the origin of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              defined by such a patch, define a smooth homotopy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi z
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau : [0,1]^3 \to X : (x,y,z) \mapsto (1-z)\Gamma(x,y) + z \Gamma'(x,y)
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi w
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z = \{(x,y,w) \in [0,1]^3 | 0 \leq w \leq \frac{1}{2}(x^2 + y^2) \}
            %p
              and consider the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : [0,1]^3 \to Z
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : (x,y,z) \mapsto (x,y, \frac{1}{2}(x^2 + y^2) z)
            %p
              and the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : Z \to X
              given away from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^2 + y^2) = 0
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mfrac
                      %mi w
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi y
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g : (x,y,w) \mapsto \tau(x,y, 2 \frac{w}{x^2 + y^2})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Using
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard%27s+lemma"} Hadamard's lemma
              and the fact that by constructon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              has vanishing 0th and 1st order differentials at the origin it follows that this is indeed a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %p
              We want to similarly factor the smooth family of bigons
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]^3 \to 2Mor(\mathbf{P}_2(X))
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [0,1]^3 \times [0,1]^2 \to X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ((x,y,z),(s,t)) \mapsto \tau(s x, t y, z)
            %p
              as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]^3 \times [0,1]^2 \to Z \times [0,1]^2 \to Z \to X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ((x,y,z),(s,t))
                    \\mapsto
                    ((x, y, \frac{1}{2}(x^2 + y^2)), (s,t))
                    \\mapsto
                    (s x , t y, \frac{1}{2}((s x)^2 + (t y)^2)z)
                    \\mapsto
                    
                    \\tau(s x, s y, z)
                    \\,.
            %p
              As before using Hadamard’s lemma this is a sequence of smooth functions. To make this qualify as a family of bigons (which are maps from the square that are constant in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              of the left and right boundary of the square) furthermore precompose this with a suitable smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]^2 \to [0,1]^2
              that realizes a square-shaped bigon.
            %p
              Under the hom-adjunction it corresponds to a factorization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\Gamma : [0,1]^3 \to 2 Mor(\mathbf{P}_2(X))
              into
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mn 3
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_\Gamma :  [0,1]^3 \stackrel{f}{\to} Z \to 2 Mor(\mathbf{P}_2(X))
                    \\,.
            %p By the above construction we have the the push-forwards
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_* : \frac{\partial}{\partial x}(x=0,y=0,z)
                    \\mapsto
                    \\frac{\partial}{\partial x}(x= 0, y = 0, w = 0)
            %p
              and similarly for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\partial}{\partial y}
              are indendent of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule"} chain rule
              that also
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{\partial^2 G_\Gamma}{\partial x \partial y}|_{(x=0,y=0)}
            %p
              is independent of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z = 0
              this equals
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi y
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\partial^2 F_\Gamma}{\partial x \partial y}|_{(x=0,y=0)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z = 1
              it equals
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ′
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi y
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\partial^2 F_{\Gamma'}}{\partial x \partial y}|_{(x=0,y=0)}
          %h4#3transport 3-Transport
          %p
            see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-groupoid+of+Lie+3-algebra+valued+forms"} 3-groupoid of Lie 3-algebra valued forms
          %h3#FlatInTop
            Flat
            = succeed "-parallel" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
          %p
            Even though it is a degenerate case, it can be useful to regard the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            explicitly a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            lots of structure of cohesive
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-theorem" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-geometric+morphism"} (∞,1)-geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Δ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Π
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi \dashv \Delta \dashv \Gamma) : Top
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Delta}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}} \in
                  \\infty Grpd
          %p
            an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+in+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid in a locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            is here the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi : Top \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \infty Grpd
                  \\,.
          %p
            If both
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by their standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            models, the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            and the standard
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} model structure on topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            is presented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
            functor in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Sing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Quillen
                    %mo ←
                  %mi Top
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (|-| \dashv Sing) : Top \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\overset{\simeq_{Quillen}}{\to}}
                  Top
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means that in this case many constructions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            and classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            have equivalent reformulations in terms of
            = succeed "-parallel" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            For instance: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Top
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(F) \in Top
            its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            = succeed "-fibrations" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Top
            are classfied by morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g : X \to B Aut(F)
          %p
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(F)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            itself is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of this cocycles, given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P &amp;\to&amp; *
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp;  B Aut(F)
                  }
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            functor we may send this equivalently to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi(P) \to \Pi(X) \to B Aut(\Pi(F))
                  \\,.
          %p
            One may think of the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X) \to B Aut(\Pi(F))
            now as the
            = succeed "-parallel" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                to each point in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                it assigns the unique object of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mi Aut
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B Aut(\Pi(F))
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                itself;
            %li
              %p
                to each path
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \to y)
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                it assigns an equivalence between the fibers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi x
                      %mi to
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_x to F_y
                etc.
          %p
            If one presents
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sing
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sing : Top \to sSet_{Quillen}
            as above, then one may look for explicit simplicial formulas that express these morphisms. Such are discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Stasheff"} Stasheff
          %p
            We may embed this example into the smooth context by regarding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(F)
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            as discussed in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#InLieGrpd"} Flat ∞-Parallel transport in Smooth∞Grpd
          %p For that purpose let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi smooth
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi smooth
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi smooth
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi LieGrpd
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi smooth
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Disc
                            %mi smooth
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mi smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi_{smooth} \dashv Disc_{smooth} \dashv \Gamma_{smooth}) :
                  \\infty LieGrpd
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi_{smooth}}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{Disc_{smooth}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma_{smooth}}{\to}}}
                  \\infty Grpd \simeq Top
          %p
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-geometric+morphism"} (∞,1)-geometric morphism
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
          %p
            We may reflect the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(F)
            into this using the
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Disc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
            to get the discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+group"} ∞-Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc Aut(F)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            = succeed "s/classifying" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Disc
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \to \mathbf{B} Disc Aut(F)
                  \\,,
          %p
            now in the smooth context of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi LieGrpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty LieGrpd
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              of
              = succeed "-fibrations" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              is equivalent to the
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Disc
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc Aut(F)
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi LieGrpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\infty LieGrpd(X, \mathbf{B} Disc Aut(F))
                    \\simeq
                    Top(X, B Aut(F))
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, all the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity%2C1)-topos#FlatDifferentialCohomology"} Flat differential cohomology
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi LieGrpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty LieGrpd
              = succeed "-transport" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi flat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_{flat}
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi Disc
                            %mi Aut
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∇
                                  %mi flat
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B} Disc Aut(F)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\nabla_{flat}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{\Pi}(X)
                    }
            %p always exists.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The first statement is a special case of that spelled out at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
              the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
          %h3#InLieGrpd
            Flat
            = succeed "-parallel" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi LieGrpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty LieGrpd
          %p (…)
          %h3#parallel_transport_from_flat_differential_forms_with_values_in_chain_complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Parallel transport from flat differential forms with values in chain complexes
          %p
            A typical choice for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-vector spaces” is that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by the a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            of modules. In a geometric context this may be replaced by some stack of complexes of vector bundles over some site.
          %p
            If we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
            for this stack, then the
            = succeed "-parallel" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{\Pi}(X) \to Mod
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is typically given by differential form data with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
          %p
            A discussion of how to integrate flat differential forms with values in chain complexes – a representation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
            as discussed at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations+of+%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroids"} representations of ∞-Lie algebroids
            – to flat
            = succeed "-parallel" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}(X) \to Mod
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#abadSchaetz"}> AbadSchaetz
            ), building on a construciton in (
            %a{:href => "#Igusa"}> Igusa
            ).
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#in_physics In physics
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            various
